{"id":"786d6bf74f2a416102d18449c157aea2595c0810","axis":"silent","repo":"open-policy-agent/opa","sha":"786d6bf74f2a416102d18449c157aea2595c0810","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -5,6 +5,56 @@ project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/)."," "," ## Unreleased"," ","+### Bundles are rooted at their `.manifest` file ([#9459](https://github.com/open-policy-agent/opa/pull/9459))","+","+Breaking change: OPA now treats the directory containing a bundle's `.manifest` file as the bundle root, as the","+[bundle documentation](https://www.openpolicyagent.org/docs/management-bundles#bundle-file-format) describes.","+Previously, the root depended on the path a bundle was loaded from, which made bundle contents, data placement,","+and signatures depend on how a path was typed.","+","+- **Bundle directories** (`opa build -b`, `opa run -b`, `opa eval -b`, `opa sign --bundle`, ...) are rooted at","+  the directory containing `.manifest`, even when it is nested below the provided path. Files above it are not","+  part of the bundle. `opa build` and `opa sign` warn about policy and data files they leave out, but other","+  commands do not, so keep other `.manifest` files (e.g., test fixtures) out of directories loaded as bundles.","+- **Bundle tarballs** loaded from disk must have `.manifest` at the root of the archive. `opa build` always writes","+  it there.","+- **Signatures**: file names in `.signatures.json` are relative to the bundle root, with `/` separators on every","+  platform. Bundles signed by `opa sign <dir>` or `opa build -b <dir>` with older OPA versions must be re-signed,","+  and `--exclude-files-verify` patterns may need updating.","+- **`opa build` with multiple bundles** places each bundle's files under the path it was given with `-b`, with a","+  new `.manifest` at the root. Leading `..` segments are replaced with the name of the directory they refer to.","+  Merging fails when two bundles would be placed under the same path. `opa sign` with multiple bundle paths","+  names files under each bundle's path, like `opa build` does when merging. A merged `opa build` output has its","+  own new `.manifest`, so signatures from multiple separate source bundles cannot be used to verify a merged build.","+- **`opa build -t plan` and `-t wasm`** replace any plan, or wasm resolvers that were carried in from the input bundles.","+- `.manifest`, `.signatures.json`, and `patch.json` must be at the bundle root, and only files named exactly","+  `.manifest` are treated as manifests.","+","+For example, consider this tarball, built without `opa build`:","+","+```console","+$ tar tzf bundle.tar.gz","+bundle/.manifest","+bundle/data.json","+bundle/authz.rego","+```","+","+Previously, `opa run -b bundle.tar.gz` loaded it with `bundle/data.json` placed under `data.bundle`. It is now","+rejected because `.manifest` is not at the root of the archive. Running `opa build -b bundle/` on the extracted","+directory produces a bundle rooted at `bundle/`, with `data.json` placed at the root of `data`.","+","+To avoid breaking existing deployments, bundles that the bundle plugin downloads over HTTP or from an OCI registry","+(and their persisted copies) are still loaded as before, and OPA logs a warning each time a bundle with a misplaced `.manifest`, `.signatures.json`,","+or `patch.json` is loaded. **These bundles will fail to load in a future OPA release.** Rebuild them with","+`opa build` to place the manifest at the root.","+","+Go API: the `bundle.Reader` expects bundle-relative descriptor paths, so directory loaders configured with the","+`SlashRooted` or `Passthrough` path formats now have their manifests rejected. When `Reader.WithBaseDir` is used,","+module paths include the manifest's directory, which directory loaders report through a `RootOffset() string`","+method. Custom loaders that wrap a directory loader should forward `RootOffset`.","+","+Authored by @philipaconrad","+"," ## 1.22.0"," "," This release contains a mix of new features, performance improvements and bug fixes. Notably:","@@ -42,7 +92,7 @@ See [Importing `rego.v2`](https://www.openpolicyagent.org/docs/policy-reference/"," "," Additionally: bundles can be declared as Rego v2 by setting the `rego_version` manifest attribute to `2` (individua "," bundle modules by setting `file_rego_versions`); and the Go API accepts the new `ast.RegoV2` rego-version when parsing,","-compiling, and formatting Rego modules. ","+compiling, and formatting Rego modules."," The `rego.v2` import is a redundant no-op for modules loaded these ways."," "," See [bundle file format](https://www.openpolicyagent.org/docs/management-bundles#bundle-file-format)."],"additions":51,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"cmd/build.go","lines":["@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ import ("," \t\"github.com/spf13/cobra\""," "," \t\"github.com/open-policy-agent/opa/cmd/internal/env\"","+\tbundleUtils \"github.com/open-policy-agent/opa/internal/bundle\""," \t\"github.com/open-policy-agent/opa/v1/ast\""," \t\"github.com/open-policy-agent/opa/v1/bundle\""," \t\"github.com/open-policy-agent/opa/v1/compile\"","@@ -344,6 +345,10 @@ func dobuild(params buildParams, args []string) error {"," \t\t}"," \t}"," ","+\tif params.bundleMode {","+\t\tbundleUtils.WarnSourcesAboveManifest(params.stderr, args, buildCommandLoaderFilter(true, params.ignore))","+\t}","+"," \tout := &deferredFileWriter{path: params.outputFile}"," \tdefer out.Close()"," "],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"cmd/build_jsonv2_test.go","lines":["@@ -1250,7 +1250,7 @@ p contains 2 if {"," \tinput.x == 1 or input.y == 2"," }`,"," \t\t\t},","-\t\t\texpManifest: `{\"revision\":\"\",\"roots\":[\"\"],\"rego_version\":1,\"file_rego_versions\":{\"%ROOT%/test2.rego\":2}}`,","+\t\t\texpManifest: `{\"revision\":\"\",\"roots\":[\"\"],\"rego_version\":1,\"file_rego_versions\":{\"/test2.rego\":2}}`,"," \t\t},"," \t\t{"," \t\t\tnote: \"v0 bundle rego-version, v1 per-file override\",","@@ -12